                         `loop -i` in a terminal asks which role and name; `loop -i dev-manager` or FACTORY_ROLE skips it.
                         On a terminal `loop -i` runs in its own tmux window (session <repo>-<name>, window
                         <role>-<name>) and shows it here; a second start of the same name says so and only shows it.
                         Without tmux it runs here, with a note
  coding-agent [name|N] loop [-i] [--once] [--dry-run] [N]
  dev-manager  [name|N] loop [-i] [--once] [--dry-run]
  product-owner [name|N] loop [-i] [--once] [--dry-run]
                         the roles, started the same way and run by the same loop (#102). The dev manager is an
                         orchestrator with no model: it watches GitHub and starts one-item sub-managers (#97). Names come
                         from roles.<role>.names; --once runs one pass, --dry-run prints what a pass would do
  init [--dry-run]       the project's scaffold: role folders, labels, the owner queue, a starter PRD and the PRD-change
